    {
      "id": 0,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Read me — if Loki panels show “No data”",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**How this dashboard reads Faro data**\n\nFaro telemetry is stored in your **Grafana Cloud Logs** Loki data source. Grafana Cloud promotes the Faro attributes `app_id`, `kind` (and `app_key`) to **labels** — there is no `app` label. Queries therefore select `{app_id=~\"$app_id\", kind=\"event\"}`.\n\n**If panels show “No data”:**\n1. Set the **Loki** data source to the `-logs` instance (name ends in `-logs`), not `…-usage-insights`.\n2. Pick your app in the **Faro app id** dropdown (All is fine). If it is empty, run `{kind=\"event\"}` in Explore — no results means frontend telemetry is not reaching this stack (check the collector URL / redeploy).\n3. Verify fields parse: `{kind=\"event\"} | logfmt | event_name=\"page_view\"` should return lines.\n\nThe **Server (Tempo)** row needs server-side OTLP env vars (`OTEL_*`) deployed; it stays empty until then."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Overview",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "panels": []
